/blog.webp

# Design-source deliverables. These are INPUTS, not build artefacts: the raw
# PNGs the designer hands over (1.4-2.8 MB each), the hand-built HTML pages the
# Figma frames were traced from, and the PDF exports. Roughly 265 MB of
# binaries - git stores each whole, and every re-delivery would add another
# full copy forever.
#
# What ships from them is already committed: the optimised WebP in
# public/tests/ and public/home/photos/ (5.5 MB total, converted at quality 82),
# and public/home/brand/. Keep these folders locally; do not commit them.
#
# /testpagesimages/ is the second batch (81 files, 145 MB) and is a DIFFERENT
# folder from /testPages/ above, not a rename - the two were delivered months
# apart and both are still referenced by docs/TEST-PAGE-IMAGES.md.
/testPages/
/testpagesimages/
/New Homepage Build/
/Women's Health - Landing Page Build/
/*.pdf
